// NEGATIVE TEST -- a macro invocation may not appear in another macro's
// ARGUMENTS (N3-12).
//
// The sibling of tests/reject/macro_invokes_macro.pd, which refuses the same
// thing written in a macro BODY. Both are the single-pass fact: the inner
// invocation is captured as argument TOKENS, spliced into the expansion, and
// the expansion is re-parsed into an AST containing a `MacroInvocation` node --
// after the pass that expands them has gone by.
//
// Measured before this refusal, and it is why the body-side check alone was not
// enough: this shape reached the type checker as "Unexpected macro invocation in
// type checking - macros should be expanded before this phase", an internal
// assertion about a compiler phase raised at the call site. The repair for both
// is expansion to a FIXED POINT, which is a change to the expansion driver.
//
// The working spelling is one line longer and is pinned in tests/03_macros.pd:
// bind the inner result to a `let`, then pass the name.
macro double!(x) { $x * 2 }

fn main() {
    print_int(double!(double!(1)));
}
